{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tensor hom adjunction tensor hom adjunction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","fileName":"Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tensor-Hom Adjunction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Projective Flat and Injective Modules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Tensor Product of Modules","Hom Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tensor hom adjunction tensor hom adjunction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","fileName":"Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tensor-Hom Adjunction","heading":"Tensor-Hom Adjunction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The tensor-Hom adjunction identifies R-linear maps M ⊗ N → P with R-linear maps M → Hom_R(N,P). A bilinear rule in two inputs can therefore be represented either by a tensor map or by a family of linear maps.\n\nThis correspondence follows from the universal property of the [[Tensor Product of Modules]]. It connects tensor constructions with the [[Hom Module]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Tensor Product of Modules","Hom Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tensor-Hom Adjunction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tensor hom adjunction tensor hom adju